# Ad-hoc scripts live in a known PLACE, not under a known NAME.
# These were previously matched as `smoke_*.py`, `check_*.py`, `verify_*.py`,
# `investigate_*.py`, `debug_*.py` - which silently excluded the migration runner,
# the migration verifier referenced eleven times in docs/, and every check written
# to prove a fix. A check that is not version controlled cannot be reviewed, cannot
# run in CI, and is gone by the next clone. Durable tooling and checks stay tracked;
# one-off probes go in backend/scripts/scratch/ (see its README).
backend/scripts/scratch/
backend/scripts/start_backend.sh
backend/scripts/start_worker.sh
backend/scripts/stop_all.sh
# Local-environment wrappers. I1c: import_local.py and migrate_auth_users.py were
# once ignored here because they embedded a service key / user password. They now
# read all credentials from the environment (like backup_cloud.py), so they are
# tracked like other durable tooling. Secrets belong in the gitignored .env only.
backend/scripts/rag_ingest_docs.py
backend/restart_wsl.sh
backend/start_both.sh
backend/start_wsl.sh
backend/stderr.log
backend/stdout.log

